    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment for new owners, formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`.\n\n**Where each piece went:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter, so the code is stored and read back on `GET`.\n\n2. **Schemas** \u2014 added a `customer_code` column to all four DB schemas (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql), matching how `email`/`registration_date` are declared.\n\n3. **`OwnerRepository`** \u2014 added a `count()` method (needed for the \"one more than current number of owners\" sequence), implemented in all three arms: `SpringDataOwnerRepository` (JPQL `@Query`, the active profile), `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`, and `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`.\n\n4. **New function class `AssignCustomerCode`** \u2014 a small single-responsibility step that reads the built `@Val Owner`, computes `LAST3` (upper-cased first three letters of the last name) and the zero-padded sequence (`count() + 1`), and sets the code. Wired into the `POST /api/owners` pipeline (under the `transaction` governance) after the registration-date default and before `save`, so the count reflects prior committed owners and the code is persisted.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema, which flows to `OwnerDto` (generated) and is mapped automatically by MapStruct by name \u2014 no mapper change needed.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` (SMI-/JON- prefixes and consecutive global sequence) passes, and the full suite is green.",
